This adapter reuses the immutable public image and launch scripts from
0xSero/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-spark-sparkinfer at commit
590d2172394dd83c1f36ff29f0dc9ec6032ea9e2 (Apache-2.0).

This adapter also includes the Apache-2.0 XGrammar 0.2.3 CPython 3.12 ARM64
wheel from PyPI, pinned by SHA-256
11255f184971489fc72b948b096e2917f482ba2dca975177f5411562cedb9c6d. It is
installed offline into the runtime virtual environment to provide the
normalize_tool_choice API required by the pinned vLLM tool parser. This
matches the upstream correction merged at
d370c0f0806a9ac994dc5f354715576cc23840b9.

Vonk supplies the exact 0xSero/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-spark snapshot from its
digest-bound artifact store at /models/weights. The adapter invokes upstream's
lossless TP4-to-TP1 coalescer, target verifier, SparkInfer self-test, and
serving launcher without downloading or modifying the published target.

The canary deliberately selects upstream's physically recorded target-only
MODE=mtp0 profile. It does not construct or load the K64 DSpark draft. Upstream
recorded 92.13 GiB loaded target weights, a 12.49 GiB padded-FP8 KV cache,
262,144-token capacity, four scheduling slots, semantic generation, and strict
JSON-schema output for that mode. The later DSpark profile recorded 95.39 GiB
after target plus draft load. Those exact records remain pinned at commit
590d2172394dd83c1f36ff29f0dc9ec6032ea9e2 under results/acceptance.json and
results/clean-image-acceptance.json.

This separate recipe remains a Candidate until the exact recipe-built image,
126 GB admission envelope, endpoint, generation, structured output, and memory
headroom pass a Vonk-managed physical Spark canary.
